2	//!
3	//! Shape of a run: poll the player for signed URLs and for the segment indexes it is holding,
4	//! download the ciphertext those URLs point at, recover the keys by testing the player's hex
5	//! candidates against that ciphertext, then decrypt and merge whatever is new. Repeat until the
6	//! lesson stops growing. Everything already decrypted is on disk, so a rerun resumes.
7	//!
8	//! The order is not arbitrary and must not be reversed. Downloading needs no key; decrypting
9	//! needs one; and a key cannot be derived until the ciphertext is on disk, because the only
10	//! derivation that works is trying candidates against the segment's own bytes. An earlier
11	//! version asked the player for keys first and then downloaded — it read them out of the
